course: dictionary
lesson: 11423
title: Quiet agreement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Acquiescence means agreeing to something quietly, without protest, even when you are not keen on it. «Her parents gave their acquiescence to the trip, though they were worried about it.» They did not shout no. They let it happen with a quiet yes.
explain: Acquiescence is about what you do, not what you feel. You can accept something and still not like it. «He gave a nod of acquiescence and went quietly to his seat.» The nod shows he agreed without an argument, even if he was not happy about it.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like quietly, without protest and even if you are not keen show that acquiescence is a calm kind of agreement. Check your meaning by swapping in "agreeing quietly" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Acquiescence is a noun, and it is uncountable. You say "acquiescence", not "an acquiescence" or "acquiescences".
fact: «With the acquiescence of» means "with someone's agreement", as in «The new road went ahead with the acquiescence of the council.»
fact: In history, «the acquiescence of the people» means the people did not resist a ruler or a law.
fact: In ethics lessons, pupils think about when silent acquiescence to unfairness is wrong, and when speaking up matters.
fact: Acquiescence is a formal word. In everyday speech you might say "agreeing quietly" or "going along with it".
exercise: «The new road went ahead with the acquiescence of the council.» What does acquiescence mean here? | Sudden anger at the council | A map of the town | Loud protest against the road | *Quiet agreement, without protest
exercise: Which phrase shows someone agreed quietly? | *A nod of acquiescence | A fierce refusal | A loud argument | A shout of joy
exercise: Ella's mum gave her acquiescence to the sleepover, though she was not keen. What does acquiescence suggest? | She was thrilled and jumped up and down | *She agreed quietly, without arguing | She was angry and left the room | She forgot all about the sleepover
test: «Silent acquiescence to unfairness can let bad things carry on.» What does silent acquiescence mean? | Writing a letter to a newspaper | Dancing at a party | *Going along with unfairness without speaking up | Shouting at the unfair rule
test: Which word is closest in meaning to acquiescence? | Argument | Refusal | *Agreement | Protest
exam: Which sentence uses acquiescence correctly? | *She gave her acquiescence with a quiet nod, though she was not keen. | Acquiescence is a fast, noisy game played outdoors. | The crowd shouted acquiescence at the referee. | The acquiescences were many and loud.
